    "updated_at": "2022-07-08T05:27:10Z",
    "body": "Hmm. This is generally something we try to avoid in web API design, by either making copies or taking ownership of the entire buffer via transferring. See https://w3ctag.github.io/design-principles/#js-rtc . (At least, I assume what you're describing would violate run to completion, since within a single event loop task, the other thread might first read one version of the buffer, then read another after the JS has updated it.)\r\n\r\nSince we don't yet have writable byte streams with ownership taking/returning semantics, we've been assuming people would make copies...",
