    "created_at": "2026-10-01T18:24:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T18:24:04Z",
    "body": "Current Chromium still appears to have the behavior described here.\n\n`SerialPortUnderlyingSink::write()` stores the original `V8BufferSource`, while `WriteData()` repeatedly creates a `DOMArrayPiece` over it and writes the remaining `ByteSpan()` into the Mojo pipe as capacity becomes available.\n\nSo bytes can still be observed incrementally rather than copied atomically when `write()` is called.\n\nThat seems worth either specifying explicitly or changing; right now implementation behavior and the safer copy-at-call-time model remain observably different.\n",
